                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                           <td>The patient’s HbA1c is elevated, indicating suboptimal long-term glycemic control and suggesting poorly controlled or undiagnosed diabetes mellitus. Clinical correlation and consideration of antidiabetic therapy adjustment or initiation are recommended. Regular monitoring and assessment for diabetes-related complications are advised.</td>
